Theorem RL-2: RC dec at last use / scope exit; ownership-transfer exclusion; unused-owned cleanup

  Preconditions:
    - RL-2 governs RcDec emission per Annex E §AIMS RC Emission:
      "RC dec SHALL be emitted at last use of an owned value or scope exit,
      UNLESS the last use is ownership-transferring (Return, Construct /
      Reuse / CollectionReuse arg, Set value, PartialApply capture, Apply /
      Invoke to an Owned param, Jump arg per the RL-4 exemption, Apply /
      Invoke to an iter-consuming param). RL-2 includes UNUSED owned
      non-scalar values (Dead / Absent) -> immediate RcDec at definition."
    - An iter-consuming param transfers ownership inward despite a Borrowed
      parameter contract: a collection passed at a borrowed terminator
      Invoke arg to a callee that iter-consumes it (`for x in coll`
      lowering -> `@iter` [owned] -> `ori_iter_drop` frees the collection
      inside the callee) is released by the callee's iterator machinery, so
      the caller emits NO dec. The distinction from a borrow-read
      (`xs.fold(..)`, does not free -> caller decs) is the proof basis: one
      terminal-use kind cannot yield both verdicts, so the iter-consuming
      kind is a DISTINCT transfer kind.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - The ownership-transfer exclusion list is the shipped predicate
      emit_rc/helpers.rs::is_ownership_transfer; last-use dec emission is
      realize/walk_dec.rs; unused-owned definitional cleanup is
      emit_rc/dead_cleanup/mod.rs (emit_dead_invoke_dsts +
      emit_dead_at_entry_decs). All routed through
      realize/mod.rs::realize_rc_reuse Sub-step B (line 140).
    - SetTag is NOT in the exclusion list — it has no value operand
      (Annex E §AIMS RL-2).
    - RL-2 applies only to HEAP-allocated values or stack-with-RC-header
      values (RL-15a Owned / MaybeShared). Headerless stack (RL-14 Unique,
      RL-15a Borrowed+Unique) gets no RC ops; cleanup is via stack-frame
      deallocation (Annex E §AIMS RL-2). This proof reasons over the
      heap / RC-header case.
    - DP-2 (is_rc_dec_unnecessary, Appendix C) gates SUPPLEMENTARY decs only
      (Cardinality = Absent OR Consumption = Dead); the terminal RL-2 /
      RL-4 / RL-5 emissions and the definitional cleanup dec own their own
      logic and are NOT suppressed by DP-2 (Annex E §AIMS DP-2 note +
      sec-8 RL-1 "DP-2 does NOT suppress definitional cleanup dec").

  Soundness property:
    Forall owned non-scalar heap value v allocated with RC = 1:

      (P1) Emission decision: at v's terminal use, RL-2 emits an RcDec iff
           the use is NOT ownership-transferring (per
           is_ownership_transfer). An ownership-transferring use hands off
           v's reference to the consumer, which inherits the dec
           obligation; emitting a dec there would double-release. An unused
           owned non-scalar (Dead / Absent) receives an immediate cleanup
           dec at definition.

      (P2) RC-count preservation: every owned non-scalar heap value is
           released exactly once — by an RL-2 last-use dec, an RL-2
           definitional cleanup dec, an RL-4 edge dec, OR an ownership
           handoff to a consumer. The net reference count returns to 0.

    RL-2 refines plain ARC by suppressing the dec on ownership-transferring
    uses (where plain ARC would dec-then-the-consumer-incs, a redundant
    pair) while preserving the same balance: the single reference moves to
    the consumer rather than being released and re-created.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1) — terminal-use decision (cross-check against
    is_ownership_transfer):

      The verifier enumerates the terminal-use kinds and asserts RL-2's
      emit-dec decision equals NOT rl2_use_transfers_ownership(kind):
        Return / ConstructArg / ReuseArg / CollectionReuseArg / SetValue /
        PartialApplyCapture / ApplyToOwnedParam / JumpArg /
        ApplyToIterConsumingParam
                                              -> NO dec (ownership transfers)
        LastReadBeforeScopeExit / ScopeExit / ApplyToBorrowedParam
                                              -> dec emitted (terminal,
                                                 non-transfer)
      Coverage gate: 12 use decisions (9 transfer + 3 non-transfer). The
      RL-2 exclusion list must match the shipped is_ownership_transfer
      exactly; any divergence fails the proof. The iter-consume GAP
      (ApplyToBorrowedParam alone cannot split the caller-dec and
      no-caller-dec verdicts) and the iter-consuming-kind soundness (a
      transfer kind -> caller emits no dec; the callee's ori_iter_drop
      releases) are discharged by the Lean mirror theorems
      RL2_iter_consuming_no_caller_dec, RL2_borrowed_param_emits_caller_dec,
      and RL2_iter_consuming_caller_dec_splits.

    Part (P2) — RC-count preservation (balance ledger):

      Sound lifecycles discharged (net = 0):
        last_use_dec_balanced — alloc, dec at last use.
        ownership_transfer_no_dec_balanced — alloc, ownership transfers out,
                                             no dec.
        unused_owned_cleanup_dec_balanced — alloc, immediate cleanup dec on
                                             an unused owned non-scalar.

    Negative-direction witnesses (REJECTED):
      NEG_dec_after_transfer_double_free — emitting a dec AFTER an ownership
                                           transfer: net = -1 (double-free).
                                           Rejected.
      NEG_unused_owned_no_cleanup_leaks — an unused owned value with no
                                           cleanup dec: net = +1 (leak).
                                           Rejected.
      Coverage gate: 5 ledger cases (3 sound + 2 negative witnesses).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl2_dec_at_last_use;
        terminal-use decision cross-check against the ownership-transfer
        model + RC-balance ledger; emits Fail on a balance violation or an
        exclusion-list divergence)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest
        RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-2 via (P1) the terminal-use dec decision cross-checked against the is_ownership_transfer exclusion list over a 12-row grid (9 transfer + 3 non-transfer, the 9th transfer kind being ApplyToIterConsumingParam) and (P2) the RC-count-preservation balance ledger (3 sound lifecycles + 2 negative-direction witnesses covering double-free and leak), grounded in the shipped realize/walk_dec.rs + emit_rc/helpers.rs is_ownership_transfer + emit_rc/dead_cleanup emission sites
